{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And He blessed</b> — the reason that HaShem needed to bless the swarming creatures of the waters, which He did not do for the creatures that emerged from the earth, and further that even among the offspring of the waters themselves He implanted jealousy, in that He did not bless the swarming bird — it appears that the matter had to be so for a necessary reason, according to what we have explained: that what HaShem commanded the waters, that they swarm, was only for that moment and not thereafter; and for the perpetuation of the species HaShem commanded that they be fruitful and multiply, for otherwise their species would perish. And since, according to the nature of the creatures that HaShem created, the power of procreation is rooted in the element of fire — for the nature of cold, on the contrary, impairs the power of generation — go out and learn from the wisdom of nature, also from their words, of blessed memory (Shabbat 156a-b), that HaShem said to Abraham: מַאי דַּעְתָּךְ דְּקָאֵי צֶדֶק וכו׳, for it is written (Isaiah 41:2): ״צֶדֶק יִקְרָאֵהוּ לְרַגְלוֹ״ — see there in their words. Accordingly, fish have no existence according to the nature fixed in creatures for procreation. Therefore HaShem returned with His august utterance and blessed them, saying — meaning, the intent of the blessing with which He blessed them is to say that they would be able to procreate, and the coldness of the water would not prevent them, nor would they need to go out of the water to warm themselves on the earth in the manner of chickens (Beitzah 7a), which sit on the ground, but within the water they would produce fruit." "And this is His saying <b>and fill the waters in the seas</b>, and it is difficult: why was it necessary to say ״in the seas״ and was it not sufficient to say ״and fill the waters״? Rather, the intent is that within the seas, there they shall swarm, and this is the blessing of the blessed One, blessed be He. And He finished saying <b>and the bird, let it multiply on the earth</b>, for it multiplies in the manner of all the earth, and this is correct."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:56:50.780643728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}